      <div class="cap" data-cap="0" hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Sign 1 of 4</p>
          <h2>Toilet</h2>
          <p>Up to pee again and again, all through the night. In a child, it can show up as wetting the bed after years of dry nights.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap" data-cap="1" hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Sign 2 of 4</p>
          <h2>Thirsty</h2>
          <p>A thirst that water doesn't fix. Glass after glass, and still dry.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap" data-cap="2" hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Sign 3 of 4</p>
          <h2>Tired</h2>
          <p>Wiped out for no reason. Asleep in the afternoon, with no energy left for the things they love.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap" data-cap="3" hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Sign 4 of 4</p>
          <h2>Thinner</h2>
          <p>Losing weight without trying, even while eating normally.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap" data-cap="4" hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Put together</p>
          <h2 class="long">Each one is easy to explain away</h2>
          <p>A hot week. A growth spurt. A busy month. But together, the four Ts mean one thing: get tested today.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap" data-cap="5" hidden>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What to do</p>
          <h2 class="long">Ask for a test today</h2>
          <p>See a doctor the same day and say you are worried about type 1 diabetes. A quick finger-prick or urine test is the first check, and it takes minutes. If it shows high sugar, more blood tests at a hospital confirm the diagnosis.</p>
          <p class="urgent"><b>Go to emergency care now if they also</b><span>are being sick, have tummy pain, are breathing fast and deep, have breath that smells fruity, or are very sleepy or confused.</span></p>
