<div class="wrap">
  <section class="after">
    <h2>The four Ts</h2>
    <p class="lede">These signs can come on over a few weeks, or much faster in young children. Any one of them is worth a test. You don't need all four.</p>
    <div class="signs">
      <div class="sign"><b>Toilet</b><span>peeing a lot, or bedwetting in a child who was dry</span></div>
      <div class="sign"><b>Thirsty</b><span>a thirst that drinking doesn't fix</span></div>
      <div class="sign"><b>Tired</b><span>wiped out for no reason</span></div>
      <div class="sign"><b>Thinner</b><span>losing weight without trying</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="urgent"><b>Go to emergency care now if they also</b><span>are being sick, have tummy pain, are breathing fast and deep, have breath that smells fruity, or are very sleepy or confused. These can be signs of diabetic ketoacidosis, which is life-threatening and needs hospital treatment.</span></p>
